Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 09:49:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 28/31] clipboard: grant a sanitized write during a gesture, as
 Chrome does

A copy button asked the application every time. Blink asks for
CLIPBOARD_SANITIZED_WRITE only when a page writes text or a known image
format during a click or a key press, and Chrome grants it by default
(components/permissions/contexts/clipboard_sanitized_write_permission_context.cc).
Qt granted it only with JavascriptCanAccessClipboard on, which also lets
document.execCommand("copy") write with no gesture at all, so an
application that wanted Chrome's answer had to take a worse one. Without
the setting, Qt reports the request as ClipboardReadWrite, the same type
as a read, and the application cannot tell the two apart.

getStatusFromSettings() now answers GRANTED for
CLIPBOARD_SANITIZED_WRITE whatever the settings say. Both callers take
it: the request a write makes, and what navigator.permissions.query()
reports for clipboard-write. CLIPBOARD_READ_WRITE, which a read and any
unsanitized or gestureless write ask for, is unchanged.

clickedWriteIsNotAsked writes from a click without a request, and checks
that the same write from a script is still asked. The clipboard-write
rows of clipboardReadWritePermissionInitialState and
clipboardReadWritePermission now expect granted, because the query asks
about a sanitized write with a gesture. The row without either setting
is listed first, because the stock run reads the first result line.

See villekivela/omaweb#745.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
